            ('What is RAG and why does it matter for enterprise AI search?', 'Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) is a method where an AI model answers from documents retrieved at question time rather than from its training data alone. For enterprise search, that means answers reflect your current policies and procedures, and each answer can point to its source. It also means you can update knowledge by changing documents instead of retraining a model. The quality of a RAG system depends more on retrieval, parsing and chunking than on which model writes the answer.'),
