            ('Can an enterprise knowledge assistant still hallucinate?', 'Yes, the risk is reduced but not eliminated. Grounding answers in retrieved passages, requiring citations and instructing the assistant to decline when retrieval finds nothing relevant all lower the rate of invented answers. Errors still happen when source documents contradict each other, are outdated or are parsed badly, such as complex tables. That’s why we score groundedness on a test set, show citations on every answer and recommend users verify high-stakes answers against the cited source.'),
